"<strong>Potential energy of a set of charges (§{#}).</strong> Bringing a charge \\(q\\) from far away to a point where the other charges make a potential \\(V\\) takes work \\(W = qV\\), and that work is stored as electric potential energy. Assembling charges one at a time therefore stores",
"\\[U = \\sum_{\\text{pairs}}\\frac{q_iq_j}{4\\pi\\epsilon_0 r_{ij}},\\]",
"one term for each pair, counted once. \\(U\\) is negative when attraction wins: then work must be done to pull the charges apart. The demo shows \\(U\\) for point charges in microjoules (\\(1\\ \\mu\\mathrm J = 10^{-6}\\) J).",
