"<strong>Potential energy.</strong> Work with the answers hidden, and calculate each energy before you show it. Start from the Triangle setup (+{#} nC at (−{#}, {#}) cm, +{#} nC at ({#}, {#}) cm, −{#} nC at ({#}, −{#}) cm) and calculate \\(U\\) of the three charges. Then take the charges away one at a time, which is the assembly run backwards: remove the −{#} nC charge, put the probe where it was and read \\(V\\) there, which gives the work needed to bring it back; then remove one +{#} nC charge and do the same. Record each step in the Potential energy table, then show the answers and check each \\(U\\). Finally, place +{#} nC and −{#} nC {#} cm apart and then {#} cm apart on the same line, and record \\(U\\) for each.",
